{"title":"Software Architect (Trainee) Roadmap","role":"Software Architect (Trainee)","summary":"A Software Architect designs the high-level structure of software systems. The role focuses on translating business and product requirements into scalable, secure, maintainable technical architectures.","facts":{"Current degree":"B.Tech / B.E.","Course":"Software Product Engineering (Industry-integrated)"},"about":[],"intro":[],"horizons":[],"sections":[{"heading":"Overview","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"Career Overview"},{"type":"p","text":"A Software Architect designs the high-level structure of software systems. The role focuses on translating business and product requirements into scalable, secure, maintainable technical architectures."},{"type":"p","text":"For a fresh graduate, “Software Architect (Trainee)” should be treated as an architecture-track entry role, rather than assuming the student will immediately own enterprise architecture. The realistic progression is usually:"},{"type":"flow","items":["B.Tech","Software Engineer / Graduate Engineer","Software Engineer","Senior Software Engineer","Technical Lead / Software Design Engineer","Solution / Software Architect","Principal Architect / Enterprise Architect"]},{"type":"p","text":"The strongest preparation is therefore deep software engineering + system design + distributed systems + cloud + architecture documentation."}]},{"heading":"Career Horizons","kind":"horizons","blocks":[{"type":"table","header":["Career Stage","Typical Focus"],"rows":[[{"text":"UG / Final Year"},{"text":"Programming, databases, APIs, software architecture fundamentals"}],[{"text":"0–2 Years"},{"text":"Software Engineer / Graduate Engineer"}],[{"text":"2–5 Years"},{"text":"Backend Engineer / Full-Stack Engineer / Senior Engineer"}],[{"text":"4–7 Years"},{"text":"Technical Lead / Software Design Engineer"}],[{"text":"6–10 Years"},{"text":"Software Architect / Solution Architect"}],[{"text":"10+ Years"},{"text":"Principal Architect / Enterprise Architect / Engineering Manager"}]]},{"type":"p","text":"A student can enter an architecture-oriented trainee program, but architecture ownership normally requires substantial engineering experience."}]},{"heading":"What to Build During the Degree","kind":"build","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"Year 1 — Strong Programming Foundation"},{"type":"h","text":"Core Programming"},{"type":"p","text":"Master at least one primary language:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Java"},{"text":"C++"},{"text":"Python"},{"text":"C#"}]},{"type":"p","text":"For this career, Java or C++ is particularly useful for understanding large-scale software systems."},{"type":"p","text":"Learn:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Object-oriented programming"},{"text":"Classes and objects"},{"text":"Interfaces"},{"text":"Inheritance"},{"text":"Polymorphism"},{"text":"Exception handling"},{"text":"Collections"},{"text":"Generics"},{"text":"File handling"},{"text":"Multithreading fundamentals"},{"text":"Memory concepts"},{"text":"Debugging"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Data Structures & Algorithms"},{"type":"p","text":"Learn:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Arrays"},{"text":"Strings"},{"text":"Linked lists"},{"text":"Stacks"},{"text":"Queues"},{"text":"Hash tables"},{"text":"Trees"},{"text":"Graphs"},{"text":"Heaps"},{"text":"Recursion"},{"text":"Sorting"},{"text":"Searching"},{"text":"Dynamic programming basics"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Target:"},{"type":"p","text":"150–250 quality DSA problems rather than merely collecting problem counts."},{"type":"h","text":"Computer Science Foundations"},{"type":"p","text":"Start:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Operating systems"},{"text":"Computer networks"},{"text":"DBMS"},{"text":"Computer architecture"},{"text":"Software engineering"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Year 2 — Software Engineering"},{"type":"p","text":"The student should transition from writing individual programs to building complete applications."},{"type":"h","text":"Learn"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Git/GitHub"},{"text":"Git branching"},{"text":"Clean code"},{"text":"SOLID principles"},{"text":"Design patterns"},{"text":"REST APIs"},{"text":"Authentication"},{"text":"Authorization"},{"text":"SQL"},{"text":"NoSQL fundamentals"},{"text":"Unit testing"},{"text":"Integration testing"},{"text":"API documentation"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Backend Development"},{"type":"p","text":"Recommended stack:"},{"type":"flow","items":["Java","Spring Boot","REST APIs","PostgreSQL / MySQL","Redis","Docker"]},{"type":"p","text":"Alternative:"},{"type":"flow","items":["C#",".NET","REST APIs","SQL Server/PostgreSQL"]},{"type":"p","text":"or"},{"type":"flow","items":["TypeScript","Node.js","REST APIs","PostgreSQL"]},{"type":"p","text":"The important objective is understanding architecture, not collecting frameworks."},{"type":"h","text":"Year 3 — System Design"},{"type":"p","text":"This is the most important transition toward architecture."},{"type":"h","text":"Learn System Design Fundamentals"},{"type":"p","text":"Understand:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Scalability"},{"text":"Availability"},{"text":"Reliability"},{"text":"Maintainability"},{"text":"Performance"},{"text":"Fault tolerance"},{"text":"Security"},{"text":"Consistency"},{"text":"Modularity"},{"text":"Coupling"},{"text":"Cohesion"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Architecture Styles"},{"type":"p","text":"Study:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Layered architecture"},{"text":"Monolithic architecture"},{"text":"Modular monolith"},{"text":"Microservices"},{"text":"Event-driven architecture"},{"text":"Serverless architecture"},{"text":"Hexagonal architecture"},{"text":"Clean architecture"},{"text":"Domain-driven design"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Understand when to use each, rather than assuming microservices are always better."},{"type":"h","text":"Year 4 — Architecture & Cloud"},{"type":"p","text":"The final year should focus on designing production-style systems."},{"type":"h","text":"Cloud"},{"type":"